WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.229 --> 00:00:02.120
(slow piano music)

00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:03.670
- I needed to give my life purpose

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:07.560
after bein' wrongfully
incarcerated for 17 years.

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:09.950
I was illiterate; I
couldn't read at the time.

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:11.570
But when I started to learn how to read,

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:14.590
it changed my life and it
actually put me in a position

00:00:14.590 --> 00:00:16.810
to be empowered enough to wanna fight

00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:18.843
for my innocence and for my freedom.

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:22.800
My name is John Bunn, and
I help promote literacy

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:23.950
in schools and prisons.

00:00:25.081 --> 00:00:28.421
(slow piano music)

00:00:28.421 --> 00:00:31.630
When I was 14 years old,
I was wrongfully accused

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:33.650
and convicted of a crime
I had no knowledge of,

00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:35.384
I had nothin' to do with.

00:00:35.384 --> 00:00:38.043
(somber music)

00:00:38.043 --> 00:00:40.777
It led to me being
incarcerated for 17 years,

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:44.210
and then on parole for another 10 years,

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:47.963
which was a total of 27 years
of me fightin' for my life.

00:00:49.088 --> 00:00:50.970
(slow piano music)

00:00:50.970 --> 00:00:53.340
In the beginnin' stages,
I was under the impression

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:55.410
that the system was gonna come to my aid

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:56.903
because I was a innocent man.

00:00:57.950 --> 00:01:00.750
The deeper I went into my incarceration,

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:02.590
the hope started to fade away.

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:04.600
When I went to trial, my lawyer told me

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:06.040
any questions or anything I had,

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:08.190
to write it down on a piece of paper.

00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:10.330
And I sat there and
couldn't write anything

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:11.920
because I didn't know
how to read and write.

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:13.040
So it was like I sat there

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:15.390
and watched my whole life
flash before my eyes.

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:19.873
So it like ignited a fire
into me to learn how to read.

00:01:21.913 --> 00:01:25.790
(upbeat orchestral music)

00:01:25.790 --> 00:01:28.140
When I was in prison,
there was a teacher there

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:30.860
that started showin' me
how to sound words out,

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:33.130
and take a special interest
in me, givin' me dictionaries

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:36.200
and children's books to
get me over the barrier.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:39.490
The process of learnin'
took about 18 months.

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:41.850
Readin' was definitely a
positive experience for me;

00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:43.273
it still is to this day.

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:46.200
I found that it was a lot of guys

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:48.280
that had this literacy issue.

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:51.030
Because of my ability to read and write,

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:52.820
I was able to help out other inmates

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:54.563
and enhance their abilities.

00:01:57.040 --> 00:01:59.206
(door rattling)

00:01:59.206 --> 00:02:00.580
(lively orchestral music)

00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:03.940
In 2018, I was able to get
that wrongful conviction

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:06.010
fully exonerated from my record,

00:02:06.010 --> 00:02:07.627
and now my life has new meanin'.

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:10.050
When I actually got released,

00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:11.920
I started A Voice 4 the Unheard,

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:14.400
which is a literacy program.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.100
It started out as a book drive.

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:18.660
I collected over 80,000 books,

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:21.130
and I distributed the books
to everywhere you can imagine,

00:02:21.130 --> 00:02:23.890
from youth detention
centers to Rikers Island

00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:26.289
to Boys Clubs to community centers.

00:02:26.289 --> 00:02:28.850
(bright orchestral music)

00:02:28.850 --> 00:02:31.390
Today, we're about to
donate thousands of books

00:02:31.390 --> 00:02:32.990
to Friends of Island Academy

00:02:32.990 --> 00:02:34.650
for them to be able to distribute.

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:37.483
And they're gonna also start
a new library in their hub.

00:02:38.770 --> 00:02:41.510
- Friends of Island Academy's
a nonprofit organization

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:43.650
offerin' advocacy, support and services

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:45.720
to age 16 to 21-year-old youth

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:48.250
affected by the criminal justice system.

00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:51.260
I met John Bunn, and immediately, I mean,

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:52.960
just connected to his story.

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:54.300
And so when I sat down with him,

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:56.480
I just felt his passion, his sincerity.

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:57.820
It wasn't a hustle; it was somethin'

00:02:57.820 --> 00:03:00.580
that was really on his heart,
to give to young people

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:03.180
and to really utilize
literacy as a tool to connect.

00:03:05.009 --> 00:03:07.780
(stately orchestral music)

00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:10.890
- Literacy is freedom,
freedom of your mind.

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:13.290
It's like you unlock your mental chain.

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:14.860
Your mind get the privilege

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:16.953
to wander the four corners of the Earth.

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:21.540
It's magical to me, to be in
a position to be privileged,

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:25.796
able enough to do somethin'
positive; that's priceless.

00:03:25.796 --> 00:03:29.337
(gentle orchestral music)

00:03:29.337 --> 00:03:32.920
(bright electronic music)

